{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/320444-need-clarification-on-how-to-use-convert-a-numina","id":320444,"title":"Need clarification on how to use/convert a Numina.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-23T22:57:46-08:00","id":320444,"title":"Need clarification on how to use/convert a Numina.","content":"Reference: MtC, p.211<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SPIRIT PROWESS: Up to five points of Essence can be reflexively and cumulatively spent to augment the ghost\u2019s Corpus (or revenant body) for a scene. One dot per point may be added to any combination of the ghost\u2019s Power, Finesse, Resilience, Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina. A reflexive expenditure of one Willpower point reallocates the bonus among Attributes. Adding to Power or Finesse does not increase a ghost\u2019s Defense. </div> </div> </div>I am assuming Resilience means Resistance - someone please correct me if I am wrong.<br /> <br /> I do not understand how a spirit is attributed Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina. I wish to use the power in a Wraith setting - or rather with ghosts, and I am wondering if I shouldn't change the reading to &quot;One dot per point may be added to any combination of the ghost's Power, Finesse, Resistance, or Corpus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Comments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T23:15:30-08:00","id":320478,"title":"","content":"The Numen in question is ported from WoD: Antagonists, where, as in Mummy, it pulls double duty as a power for revenants, which have a mortal complement of Traits, including the nine-Attribute set that contains Strength, Dexterity, and Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T05:48:24-08:00","id":320645,"title":"","content":"There's also the Lucid Dead Numen, which grants a ghost full &quot;personhood&quot; and also the nine-Attribute suite.<br /> <br /> It's on page 209 of MtC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edite